\newlabel{tab:fusion-variants}{{2}{8}{Decision-level variants for the focused backbone (\model {sensitiveai-vi-custom}) on test. Every variant reads the same frozen scores; only mixing and the decision rule differ; the last row is primary. \emph {Per-class columns are F1}; best macro-F1 in bold. Rule-only rows are scored inside the fusion pipeline on renormalised rule scores; the standalone engine with its own thresholds is reported in the text}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Quantitative summary for the focused backbone. (a)\ Macro-F1 of every decision variant; the dotted line is AI-only, the green bar the per-channel hybrid. (b)\ Provenance of the 38 changed decisions, by correction and regression type. (c)\ Behaviour of the rule channel on test: coverage, precision when firing, recall on non-\textsc  {clean}{} comments, and false alarms on \textsc  {clean}{}; values are percentages, raw counts are in the text.}}{8}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:results}{{2}{8}{Quantitative summary for the focused backbone. (a)\ Macro-F1 of every decision variant; the dotted line is AI-only, the green bar the per-channel hybrid. (b)\ Provenance of the 38 changed decisions, by correction and regression type. (c)\ Behaviour of the rule channel on test: coverage, precision when firing, recall on non-\clean {} comments, and false alarms on \clean {}; values are percentages, raw counts are in the text}{figure.2}{}}
